<section
  class="home-engagement wrap"
  id="engagements"
  aria-labelledby="engagement-title"
>
  <div class="home-engagement-intro">
    <p class="kicker">Working together</p>
    <h2 id="engagement-title">An engineer who stays with the work.</h2>
    <p>
      We embed with your team, work through the problem in its real setting, and
      carry the build through review and handover.
    </p>
    <a class="quiet-link" href="#contact"
      >Discuss your project <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
    >
  </div>
  <ol class="home-engagement-steps">
    <li>
      <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
      <div>
        <p class="small-label">Paid first phase</p>
        <h3>Define the result together.</h3>
        <p>
          We look at the actual process with your team and choose the work to
          take on. Scope and price are agreed before work starts. You keep the
          findings if you stop here.
        </p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
      <div>
        <p class="small-label">Delivery</p>
        <h3>Build where your team works.</h3>
        <p>
          We build in your environment, with checks against the agreed result.
          Your team reviews every change and approves what gets merged.
        </p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
      <div>
        <p class="small-label">Handover</p>
        <h3>You keep the result.</h3>
        <p>
          The engagement has a defined end. Your team keeps the delivered work,
          source, and findings. Further work is a decision you make at the
          checkpoint.
        </p>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ol>
